WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.446 --> 00:00:02.326
- By being a racing driver,

00:00:02.326 --> 00:00:04.193
you are under risk all the time.

00:00:04.193 --> 00:00:07.153
I use those lines and those guidelines

00:00:07.153 --> 00:00:09.394
to move as a man, as a professional.

00:00:09.394 --> 00:00:12.500
I like to do well, I like to be the best.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.917
I am as, committed as ever to my passion.

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:21.433
Everyone is responsible for
the race having being started.

00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:23.698
I am only 32 and it's
no sense for me to stop.

00:00:23.698 --> 00:00:27.865
- [Announcer] (commentates in Portuguese)

00:00:33.005 --> 00:00:34.502
(car engines roaring)

00:00:34.502 --> 00:00:35.884
- He's a Brazilian race driver

00:00:35.884 --> 00:00:38.878
who won three Formula
One world championships.

00:00:38.878 --> 00:00:40.155
- He was killed in an accident

00:00:40.155 --> 00:00:44.113
while leading the 1994
San Marino Grand Prix.

00:00:44.113 --> 00:00:45.343
- He's considered by many as

00:00:45.343 --> 00:00:48.270
the greatest race car driver of all time.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.077
- He's Ayrton Senna,

00:00:50.077 --> 00:00:53.577
and here are his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:58.280
(music)

00:01:06.557 --> 00:01:09.630
- You should know that
by being a racing driver,

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.095
you are under risk all the time.

00:01:12.095 --> 00:01:13.849
By being a racing driver means,

00:01:13.849 --> 00:01:15.886
you are racing with other people.

00:01:15.886 --> 00:01:18.735
And if you no longer go
for a gap that exists,

00:01:18.735 --> 00:01:20.445
you no longer a racing driver,

00:01:20.445 --> 00:01:23.728
because we are competing,
we are competing to win.

00:01:23.728 --> 00:01:26.053
And the main motivation to all of us,

00:01:26.053 --> 00:01:27.903
is to compete for victory.

00:01:27.903 --> 00:01:30.514
It's not to come third,
fourth, fifth or sixth.

00:01:30.514 --> 00:01:34.681
- [Interviewer] (speaks in Portuguese)

00:01:39.406 --> 00:01:43.573
- [Ayrton] (speaks in Portuguese)

00:02:22.195 --> 00:02:24.982
I have had all my life a very,

00:02:24.982 --> 00:02:27.656
very strong and good education.

00:02:27.656 --> 00:02:30.768
And from that education I've got, again,

00:02:30.768 --> 00:02:34.685
clear and strong principals
in way of behaving.

00:02:35.973 --> 00:02:38.250
And that's where I guide for...

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:42.163
I use those lines and those guidelines

00:02:42.163 --> 00:02:45.163
to move as a man, as a professional.

00:02:47.089 --> 00:02:49.455
And I don't regret anything,

00:02:49.455 --> 00:02:53.622
I just feel I'm doing
things for the right reason.

00:02:55.258 --> 00:02:57.966
Some understand, some don't.

00:02:57.966 --> 00:03:00.226
In the end you never get
everybody to understand,

00:03:00.226 --> 00:03:02.316
to agree and to accept.

00:03:02.316 --> 00:03:04.566
But most of them, I'm sure,

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.667
admire after all, what I'm doing

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:12.434
as a professional and as a man

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:15.430
and as many drivers do.

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:19.640
We are exposing our lives,
they are consistent.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.634
And the reason for it is only one,

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.411
it's to succeed, it's to win.

00:03:23.411 --> 00:03:27.156
It's to get the thrill when
you cross the finish line

00:03:27.156 --> 00:03:28.649
in first place.

00:03:28.649 --> 00:03:29.944
I am very competitive.

00:03:29.944 --> 00:03:32.027
I think any racing driver

00:03:34.031 --> 00:03:36.114
that gets to Formula One,

00:03:37.087 --> 00:03:41.170
has in expressionality,
a lot of competitiveness.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:48.347
I particularly believe to
be extremely competitive

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.613
in anything I do.

00:03:55.678 --> 00:03:59.669
But it depends where you
are and what you're doing

00:03:59.669 --> 00:04:01.412
and what is your state of mind.

00:04:01.412 --> 00:04:04.540
If I'm on holiday, off season,

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:07.068
it's a different way of living totally

00:04:07.068 --> 00:04:09.704
then when you do interviews,

00:04:09.704 --> 00:04:11.058
when you're testing,

00:04:11.058 --> 00:04:12.307
you're in the season of racing,

00:04:12.307 --> 00:04:13.501
competing during the season.

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:17.668
You have to allow yourself
different mental approach,

00:04:19.261 --> 00:04:21.428
a different way of looking

00:04:22.906 --> 00:04:24.406
the day and night.

00:04:25.561 --> 00:04:28.270
And only that way I find possible

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.937
to get the necessary equilibrium

00:04:31.773 --> 00:04:35.837
to then give everything I
have when it really matters.

00:04:35.837 --> 00:04:38.304
But in normal things I am competitive.

00:04:38.304 --> 00:04:41.788
I like to compete and I like to do well.

00:04:41.788 --> 00:04:43.703
I like to be the best.

00:04:43.703 --> 00:04:47.870
- [Ayrton] (speaks in Portuguese)

00:05:25.885 --> 00:05:29.455
- Ayrton, it has been a quite
incredible season for you.

00:05:29.455 --> 00:05:33.378
You are the youngest ever
three times world champion,

00:05:33.378 --> 00:05:36.239
three times in four years.

00:05:36.239 --> 00:05:40.936
I have to ask you on behalf
of your despairing rivals.

00:05:40.936 --> 00:05:44.353
Is your motivation still as high as ever?

00:05:47.226 --> 00:05:50.643
- I think so. (laughter)

00:05:55.214 --> 00:05:58.214
I am as you said, young and healthy.

00:06:00.555 --> 00:06:02.638
I am as committed as ever

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:07.850
to my passion, to our passion,

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:10.315
and to my profession.

00:06:10.315 --> 00:06:13.482
And the main thing is to find the ways

00:06:17.056 --> 00:06:19.973
time after time to stimulate myself

00:06:21.787 --> 00:06:24.704
in my own world, my own funny ways.

00:06:27.989 --> 00:06:32.156
To dedicate a lot of my time
and a lot of my thinking

00:06:33.086 --> 00:06:35.669
and keep up when the commitment

00:06:39.424 --> 00:06:43.091
is quite high to continue,
to be successful.

00:06:45.017 --> 00:06:47.014
- (Reporter) If we were to
run into rain conditions

00:06:47.014 --> 00:06:50.267
of this kind again, is
there a better method,

00:06:50.267 --> 00:06:52.988
Ayrton, for us to look into how the race

00:06:52.988 --> 00:06:55.044
should be stopped, earlier or more--

00:06:55.044 --> 00:06:58.504
- We shouldn't start. (crosstalk)

00:06:58.504 --> 00:07:00.948
I think it's very hard
for the officials to make

00:07:00.948 --> 00:07:03.414
such a decision, because
there is a lot of pressure.

00:07:03.414 --> 00:07:05.662
Television all over the world, and...

00:07:05.662 --> 00:07:07.426
And it's difficult, we understand.

00:07:07.426 --> 00:07:09.811
But I think it's, in a
way, it's our own fault.

00:07:09.811 --> 00:07:11.821
We shouldn't have started as drivers,

00:07:11.821 --> 00:07:14.979
if we just get out of
the cars, stick together,

00:07:14.979 --> 00:07:16.834
and make a decision for ourselves,

00:07:16.834 --> 00:07:19.579
then the race wouldn't
start in the first place.

00:07:19.579 --> 00:07:22.125
It's always very difficult
to get everyone together,

00:07:22.125 --> 00:07:25.395
I've experienced it myself
two years ago, today again,

00:07:25.395 --> 00:07:28.242
because also we have a
lot of responsibility

00:07:28.242 --> 00:07:31.499
to the teams and the sponsors
that give us so much,

00:07:31.499 --> 00:07:34.125
and there are moments that we have to also

00:07:34.125 --> 00:07:36.323
try to give them some simple--

00:07:36.323 --> 00:07:37.933
it's very difficult to find equilibrium

00:07:37.933 --> 00:07:40.058
to balance on making the right decisions

00:07:40.058 --> 00:07:42.281
at every single time, but as I said,

00:07:42.281 --> 00:07:46.613
I think it was a mistake to
all of us to have started.

00:07:46.613 --> 00:07:49.586
Not only from the officials,
it was also driver's mistake,

00:07:49.586 --> 00:07:53.753
was team's mistake, we all
should have courage as a group.

00:07:55.171 --> 00:07:59.084
Everyone that is here to get
together and go against it,

00:07:59.084 --> 00:08:01.587
and not start the race.

00:08:01.587 --> 00:08:05.252
So it's not officials only,
I also take responsibility,

00:08:05.252 --> 00:08:07.696
as drivers, and also the team--

00:08:07.696 --> 00:08:10.802
everyone is responsible for
the race having been started.

00:08:10.802 --> 00:08:15.246
I expressed the feeling some
time ago, a couple months ago

00:08:15.246 --> 00:08:20.228
that I wouldn't be prepared
to continue driving next year,

00:08:20.228 --> 00:08:23.811
unless I felt I could
compete--competitive,

00:08:25.006 --> 00:08:28.820
and that meant not that I had
to leave McLaren or anything,

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.583
it just meant if you feel you have

00:08:31.583 --> 00:08:33.405
some light at the end
of the tunnel in which

00:08:33.405 --> 00:08:37.572
you can work and make up, and
be back in a compeititve way.

00:08:39.598 --> 00:08:42.348
And if that situation, did not...

00:08:45.615 --> 00:08:49.172
Turn up for me, then I wouldn't drive.

00:08:49.172 --> 00:08:50.810
Without really wishing to stop,

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:55.453
because I am only 32, and it
is no sense for me to stop,

00:08:55.453 --> 00:08:56.899
I mean, the peak of my career is

00:08:56.899 --> 00:08:59.978
still with quite few years ahead.

00:08:59.978 --> 00:09:03.604
I have achieved so much
credibility, so much experience,

00:09:03.604 --> 00:09:07.810
that is it's not the time to
stop, but on the other hand,

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:11.761
there's absolutely no sense
to just be a number out there,

00:09:11.761 --> 00:09:14.450
giving the fact that whether
you're fighting for first

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:18.363
or second, or fifth or sixth,
you just expose yourself

00:09:18.363 --> 00:09:22.446
to a lot of danger
continuously, a lot of stress,

00:09:23.362 --> 00:09:27.529
and a lifestyle that not
always is attractive for me.

00:09:28.918 --> 00:09:31.751
Therefore, considering everything,

00:09:33.218 --> 00:09:36.001
the material benefits I got up until now,

00:09:36.001 --> 00:09:38.801
and the ones I could get in the future,

00:09:38.801 --> 00:09:41.427
the personal satisfaction,

00:09:41.427 --> 00:09:44.035
the achievements that you can get,

00:09:44.035 --> 00:09:46.582
and the only real motivation
for me to continue

00:09:46.582 --> 00:09:50.354
was to be in a position where
I could compete, improve,

00:09:50.354 --> 00:09:52.354
learn more and be there.

00:09:53.232 --> 00:09:56.760
Be there fighting at least for it.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:00.843
And anything else, I could
not justify to myself.

00:10:02.001 --> 00:10:05.751
(Ayrton speaking Portuguese)

00:10:51.116 --> 00:10:53.644
(crowd cheering)

00:10:53.644 --> 00:10:57.811
- [Reginaldo] (speaking Portuguese)

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:13.017
- [Announcer] (commentates in Portuguese)

00:11:29.304 --> 00:11:31.754
- [Ron] Ayrton pulled out in the lead,

00:11:31.754 --> 00:11:35.921
he was then really faced
with a very easy race win.

00:11:42.821 --> 00:11:46.988
- [Announcer] (speaks Portuguese)

00:11:48.872 --> 00:11:51.304
- [Ron] And then, the gearbox jammed,

00:11:51.304 --> 00:11:55.032
and he was faced with several laps to go,

00:11:55.032 --> 00:11:57.282
only having the sixth gear.

00:11:59.778 --> 00:12:03.945
- [Reginaldo] (speaks in Portuguese)

00:12:27.012 --> 00:12:31.179
- [Announcer] (commentates in Portuguese)

00:12:49.316 --> 00:12:52.399
- [Ayrton] (screams)

00:13:11.861 --> 00:13:14.611
(crowd cheering)

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:32.317
- [Reginaldo] (speaks Portuguese)

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:58.417
- [Ayrton] (speaks Portuguese)

00:14:13.848 --> 00:14:15.154
- Thank you so much for watching,

00:14:15.154 --> 00:14:18.603
we made this video because
Devesh Somani asked us to.

00:14:18.603 --> 00:14:19.687
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:14:19.687 --> 00:14:21.577
that you want us to profile next,

00:14:21.577 --> 00:14:22.685
leave it in the comments below,

00:14:22.685 --> 00:14:23.874
and we'll see what we can do.

00:14:23.874 --> 00:14:26.608
- We would love to know which
one of his top ten rules

00:14:26.608 --> 00:14:29.056
that you like the most,
please leave a comment below

00:14:29.056 --> 00:14:30.931
before joining the discussion.

00:14:30.931 --> 00:14:33.459
- Thank you guys for
watching, continue to believe,

00:14:33.459 --> 00:14:35.959
and we'll see you soon.
- Bye!

